From fe7c0eddd17ad472b8969bfb0337e76ea4bfe911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 17:05:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 21/38] fix(int4-onnx): kBF16 enum is 7 not 5 (5 is kUINT8)

The BF16-output dispatch emitted output_dtype=5 thinking it was kBF16, but
nvinfer1::DataType 5 is kUINT8 (kBF16=7). TensorRT rejected the plugin output
as an illegal UINT8 intermediate ('legalUINT8' assertion) at the down_proj
node. The plugin C++ used the symbolic enum (correct); only the ONNX attribute
value was wrong. Now emits 7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013XsZpWRubKjuZDyZqx3q4E

diff --git a/tensorrt_edgellm/onnx/dynamo_translations.py b/tensorrt_edgellm/onnx/dynamo_translations.py
index 1476109..4ce153c 100644
--- a/tensorrt_edgellm/onnx/dynamo_translations.py
+++ b/tensorrt_edgellm/onnx/dynamo_translations.py
@@ -266,9 +266,11 @@ def _int4_groupwise_gemm_translation(
     )
 
 
-# nvinfer1::DataType::kBF16 == 5 (TensorRT enum). The plugin reads this int32
-# attribute and routes to the FP32-accumulate / BF16-store kernels.
-_TRT_DATATYPE_BF16 = 5
+# nvinfer1::DataType::kBF16 == 7 (TensorRT enum: kFLOAT=0 kHALF=1 kINT8=2 kINT32=3
+# kBOOL=4 kUINT8=5 kFP8=6 kBF16=7). The plugin reads this int32 attribute and routes
+# to the FP32-accumulate / BF16-store kernels. (NOTE: 5 is kUINT8 — using it makes
+# TensorRT reject the plugin output as an illegal UINT8 intermediate.)
+_TRT_DATATYPE_BF16 = 7
 
 
 @script()
